Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||07-29-2000||05:10 PM||||I'll try to make it short.<P>I got a virus a while back (KaK worm) then bought Norton antivirus and got rid of it. I still have a blank page that comes up each time I reboot though. It says "kakstartup" or something like that. Obviously part of the virus I had. I go to start, programs, and then startup and see the kakstartup thing. I delete it but it still returns with each reboot. I scanned that with Norton and found nothing wrong with it, but it shouldn't be there. This is not really my problem, just one of the long list.<P>Here is my big problem.<BR>I like to play games online at the Gaming Zone. Now when I go there I get a page saying my browser in not supported. I then went and downloaded IE 5.5... same thing. I then try to locate the program (IE5.5) under <B>start, settings, control panel, add/remove programs</B>. It's not there, so I redownload IE 5.5. Still not working. I then went to Netscape to download their browser and it tells me I have IE 5.5??? What the hell is wrong with this computer??<P>Thanks in advance....<p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 07-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||07-29-2000||07:12 PM||||Sounds like the virus wrote to the windows registry. It doesn't mean the virus is still active, just means you have to take that line out of the register. Be careful, delete or change the wrong thing and your screwed. I don't know quite enough about how to do that to talk you through it. You might try going to the Norton site, usually they have detailed info on how to restore you machine back from a virus.<P>I went through that same thing with the Gaming Zone a couple months ago when they did a bunch of upgrades. I tried a bunch of thing and couldn't get any support from MSN. Finally, after about three days, everything was back to normal. I did find a way to force my way in during this time, but I can't remember how I did it. Through one of the pull down menus in one of the small windows or something like that. Next time I get back to Fighter Ace, I'll try to figure it out for you.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||07-29-2000||10:12 PM||||I had a few friends hit by this virus. Go to the link below and type in the virus name. The page and info on the virus will tell you EXACTLY how to get the little bugger out of your registry and it has a link to get a patch so you won't get it via Email anymore.<BR>This is the best anti-virus site I have found. Excellent support and they usually have a patch or instructions on removing the virus before anyone else!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.f-secure.com/virus-info/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.f-secure.com/virus-info/</A> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 07-29-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000003||GT Bastard||07-30-2000||01:57 PM||||About the message you see on boot...<P>to to start/run/ and type "win.ini" without the quotes.  When you click ok, a notepad window will pop up with the win.ini file.  Towards the top of this document, look for a line that says "load=" and "run=" If there is anything resembling kak after the "=" sign in either one, delete it(only delete what is after the "=" sign on that line though.)  Save the file and restart.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||07-30-2000||05:53 PM||||SCCA, on the Gaming Zone thing, if you can get that ZoneFriends window, pull down one of the menus and try log on as...||||reg||1
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||07-31-2000||04:53 AM||||GT Bastard, thanks for the tip, but I got that part taken care of. I went to Norton's site and followed their instructions and it worked somewhat. I still have a page come up when I signon online that says "Browser not supported" but I can surf the web just fine... except for the Gaming Zone and MSN's homepage. (actually I can get to MSN's homepage, but when I sign online it won't come up.)<P>batboy, the sign-on for my Zone Friends won't even come up. I can go into the parts that gives me choices of rooms to go in, but when I click on one of the rooms is when I get the "Browser not supported" page.<P>Stupid computer.<p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 07-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroSTETZ||08-01-2000||02:35 AM||||try clicking "start&gt;run&gt;msconfig" go to startup, and remove any reference to kak. at compUSA we use this on many customers units, especially compaq's (loaded with so many TSR's that the resources hoveraround 55-60%)||||reg||1
